---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { project, sourceUrl, verification } from '../data/project';
---
<Base title="Releases" description="Read the published Scarp alpha milestone, source baseline, downloads, verification record, and upstream changelog.">
  <section class="wrap page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Releases & changelog</p><h1>Every milestone.<br />A little further.</h1><p class="lead">Published snapshots of a language in development.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap release-entry"><div><span class="status-badge">Experimental prerelease</span><p class="mono">1 November 2026</p><h2>v{project.version}</h2></div><div class="prose"><h3>Source modules</h3><p>Relative <code>.srp</code> imports, explicit aliases, public functions and scalar literal constants, bounded source graphs, and cycle diagnostics.</p><p>Builds on the existing numerical runtime, immutable tiles, function contracts, and independent execution budgets.</p><ul><li>Windows x64 MSVC</li><li>Linux x64 GNU</li><li>macOS ARM64</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/downloads/">Get this release →</a><a class="inline-link" href={project.release}>Full release notes ↗</a></div><p><a href={verification}>Publication and package verification ↗</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section prose"><h2>Release history</h2><p>The compiler repository maintains the complete <a href={`${project.repo}/releases`}>release archive</a> and <a href={sourceUrl('CHANGELOG.md')}>changelog through this baseline</a>. Older examples and binary packages can use different syntax or lack newer features.</p><h2>Version-aware learning</h2><p>Use the website’s v{project.version} examples with that interpreter version. This page is a reviewed snapshot, not an automatic feed of unpublished work. No stable release is represented by this baseline.</p></section>
</Base>
